;; a64i's $GOROOT/test check's classes (bin/a64i goroot-check; doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md "As built: AR24"): every row of
;; test/asm/a64i-goroot-results-arm64.edn that does not pass is in one of these. In goi's format. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :gc-arm64
  :title "gc's own run on arm64 does not pass the test"
  :kind :design
  :why "the reference is this M2's run of the program gc built for linux/arm64; where it does not pass the test itself (a status, an output not the golden .out's: the corpus's tests that need a GOEXPERIMENT, cgo, or the amd64 record's environment) a64i's run is held to the CPU's alone, and equal to it"
  :decided "AR24"}
 {:id :not-arm64
  :title "a program not for linux/arm64"
  :kind :design
  :why "its //go:build line, as Go's test driver evaluates it (shouldTest), excludes linux/arm64 without cgo: the driver does not run it"
  :decided "AR24"}
 {:id :driver-skip
  :title "a program goi's check does not run so"
  :kind :design
  :why "its action sets -goexperiment or -godebug (goi's check skips those), or the CPU's own run timed out: no reference"
  :decided "AR24"}
 {:id :speed
  :title "speed: a program over a64i's budget"
  :kind :budget
  :why "a64i interprets A64 one instruction at a time, a thousand times slower than the M2 (2-15 M instructions a second against its billions): a program whose CPU run takes over A64I_GOROOT_CPU_MAX ms (1000) is not run on a64i, and one that ran over its budget (A64I_GOROOT_TMO, 120 s) is named in test/asm/a64i-goroot/known.edn and not run again; a budget's failure, not a divergence"
  :decided "AR24"}
]
